{"asks":[{"quote":"If you disagree, say so and I'll add it under Appearance.","question":"Should the activity strip have an Appearance preference?","kind":"decision","options":["Keep no preference","Add Appearance toggle"]},{"quote":"Do you want Strata to normalize these, for example always showing \"Explore: search for tests\" style labels, or should it show what the provider sent?","question":"Should Strata normalize subagent labels or display provider-supplied labels?","kind":"decision","options":["Normalize labels","Show provider labels"]},{"quote":"Tell me which you'd rather see and I'll do that one.","question":"Should finished activity stay under messages or move into the Trace drawer?","kind":"decision","options":["Keep under message","Move to Trace drawer"]},{"quote":"Is eight the right number, or would you rather it show everything and scroll?","question":"Should the strip show eight rows or all rows with scrolling?","kind":"decision","options":["Eight visible rows","Show all with scrolling"]},{"quote":"I'm treating a subagent that errors as finished, with a red dot, and not surfacing its error text in the strip. The error is in the trace. Is that enough, or do you want the error inline?","question":"Should subagent errors remain only in Trace or appear inline in the activity strip?","kind":"decision","options":["Trace only","Show inline"]},{"quote":"The elapsed timer stops when T3 reports completion, not when the parent turn ends. That means a subagent that finished early keeps showing its own short time. I think that's correct.","question":"Should elapsed timers stop at each subagent's completion?","kind":"question","options":[]},{"quote":"The strip doesn't show token usage per subagent. T3 does report it, so it's available. I left it out because the usage panel already totals it and per-row numbers made the strip busy. I can add it back if it's useful to you.","question":"Should each subagent row include token usage?","kind":"decision","options":["Leave out","Show per-row usage"]},{"quote":"Let me know if you'd rather I hold this until the link-opening change lands, since both touch the Conversation panel and there's a small merge risk in the message component.","question":"Should this work wait until the link-opening change lands?","kind":"decision","options":["Continue now","Hold until link change"]}]}
